  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nIncreased moisture from Lake Erie is resulting in fog, some of which\nis dense, across portions of northern/northwest Ohio. The light \nnortheast flow is pushing the fog into Hardin County Ohio, and it \nwill continue to expand over the next few hours into daybreak. Given \nthe expected expansion, a dense fog advisory has been issued for \nareas that will also see dense fog develop. Additional counties will \nbe added as needed. \n\nOtherwise, some pockets of fog are expected elsewhere, along with\nlocal rivers and valleys. \n\nA similar situation may occur tomorrow, with fog occurring across\nportions of west-central Ohio. \n\nKey Message 2)\n\nHigh pressure remains in place across the eastern CONUS through the\nend of the week, reinforced by another ridge into the weekend. High\ntemperatures are few degrees above normal, and dry conditions will\npersist. Some occasions of frost, primarily across central and \nsouth- central Ohio are possible with temperatures dropping into the \nmid 30s Wednesday night and Friday night. \n\nOtherwise, increasing mid and upper level will try to bring an\nincrease in cloud cover this weekend into early next week. A pattern\nchange may finally enter the region early-middle of next week as a \ntrough moves into the Great Lakes.",
